{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l1nx24i5","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"physics","chapter":"waves","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"doppler-effect","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"ptwo-vehicles-each-moving-with-speed-u-on-the-same-horizo-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-0nkd3rl6fzkzfwnv","content":"<p>Two vehicles, each moving with speed u on the same horizontal straight road, are approaching each other. Wind blows along the road with velocity w. One of these vehicles blows a whistle of frequency f<sub>1</sub>. An observer in the other vehicle hears the frequency of the whistle to be f<sub>2</sub>. The speed of sound in still air is V. The correct statement(s) is(are)</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"If the wind blows from the observer to the source, f<sub>2</sub> > f<sub>1</sub>."},{"identifier":"B","content":"If the wind blows from the source to the observer, f<sub>2</sub> > f<sub>1</sub>."},{"identifier":"C","content":"If the wind blows from the observer to the source, f<sub>2</sub> < f<sub>1</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"If the wind blows from the source to the observer, f<sub>2</sub> < f<sub>1</sub>."}],"correct_options":["A","B"],"explanation":"<p>Doppler's effect gives</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.469ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"14.352ex\" height=\"4.07ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1149.5 6343.6 1799\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(523,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1204.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(2260.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"5B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-LO-5B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(472,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,457.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(485,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1263,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D462\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D462\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(605,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(227.8,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(485,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1263,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D462\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D462\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(605,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D460\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D460\"></use></g></g></g></g><rect width=\"1806.2\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2518.2,0) translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"5D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-LO-5D\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(5417,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(523,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ..... (1)</p>\n<p>Let the wind speed be w and wind moves towards the source in case (i) and towards the observer in case (ii) (see figure).</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qhjpun/f757e339-ddcb-44de-98c3-2b0980440570/d5c2a2f0-b742-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qhjpuo.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1qhjpun/f757e339-ddcb-44de-98c3-2b0980440570/d5c2a2f0-b742-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qhjpuo.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Waves Question 27 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1qhjpun/f757e339-ddcb-44de-98c3-2b0980440570/d5c2a2f0-b742-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qhjpuo.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1qhjpun/f757e339-ddcb-44de-98c3-2b0980440570/d5c2a2f0-b742-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qhjpuo.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qhjpun/f757e339-ddcb-44de-98c3-2b0980440570/d5c2a2f0-b742-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qhjpuo.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1qhjpun/f757e339-ddcb-44de-98c3-2b0980440570/d5c2a2f0-b742-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qhjpuo.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1qhjpun/f757e339-ddcb-44de-98c3-2b0980440570/d5c2a2f0-b742-11ec-885a-17f955768420/file-1l1qhjpuo.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1qhjpun/f757e339-ddcb